{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/274612-open-development-alchemical-recipes","id":274612,"title":"Open Development: Alchemical Recipes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-07T05:09:51-07:00","id":274612,"title":"Open Development: Alchemical Recipes","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/alchemical-recipes/\" target=\"_blank\">Read it here.</a><br /> <br /> I'm excited to explore the Extempore, but I'm sad to see that the Zeka aren't making a reappearance. I'm guessing they were cut for word count reasons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T05:27:42-07:00","id":274649,"title":"","content":"Apparently, Matt wants to do them if Promethean ever gets a Night Horrors book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T06:05:28-07:00","id":274668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merkonan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/274612-open-development-alchemical-recipes?p=274649#post274649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently, Matt wants to do them if Promethean ever gets a Night Horrors book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad to hear that Matt has plans. Where'd you hear about this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T06:31:35-07:00","id":274685,"title":"","content":"From Matt, in one of the recent 2e threads to be found on this board.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T07:16:04-07:00","id":274703,"title":"","content":"Fantastic.<br /> <br /> I guess my only other concern is that it seems like the Unfleshed are taking the spot of Constructs. I guess Golems and Galateans just make more sense to me as built-from-scratch rather than being animated bodies. I notice you also express this view in the other open dev thread, Dataweaver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T07:20:57-07:00","id":274707,"title":"","content":"yeah!!!!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T10:14:38-07:00","id":274820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/274612-open-development-alchemical-recipes?p=274703#post274703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess my only other concern is that it seems like the Unfleshed are taking the spot of Constructs. I guess Golems and Galateans just make more sense to me as built-from-scratch rather than being animated bodies. I notice you also express this view in the other open dev thread, Dataweaver.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of us had similar views. I think that what their bodies are physically made of is the least interesting way to define a Lineage. The terracotta warriors were designed to be soldiers in the afterlife. Pinnochio or David from A.I. were created specifically to be a loving child. I can't see &quot;not made of flesh&quot; as a sufficent justification to say those are the same Lineage or even the same humour. I'd make David Sanguine. (In fact; I would say that the majority of robots in non-Promethian media who want to become human were Sanguine, not Oil - to go by Oil's short description)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-07-2014, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T10:44:44-07:00","id":274842,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's really enough information to get a clear idea of how Unfleshed will work in relation to the others. Considering that two of the Big 5 are based on literal golems/statues, plus the description of the oil humor, I'm not entirely sure anything not made of people will automatically fall under the Unfleshed tent. Also if Galateans and Tammuz become more construct-y, we'll have 3 made of people splats and 3 made of stuff splats, plus Extemporae as the wild card. Plus, of the Big 5, Galateans and Tammuz disfigurements work a bit better conceptually when the character isn't made of flesh, anyway.<br /> <br /> On the other side of the argument, The Unfleshed is about as clear a name as you can get for construct related stuff. Plus the bit about golems and terracotta warriors.<br /> <br /> Again though, until we get a bit more info from the Q&amp;A session, its hard to tell where things stand. Personally I hope the Unfleshed stay as machines (or similar constructs) with the others embodying stuff like statues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T10:51:11-07:00","id":274852,"title":"","content":"I agree that we don't have much evidence - I'm just going by the little bit that we do have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T12:07:02-07:00","id":274911,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t mind the Unfleshed being folded into Constructs; what bothers me is that they\u2019re being turned into a Lineage. I think what I\u2019d most like to see next is a write-up (even a tentative one) of the Unfleshed, somethng to explain why the writers feel it will work better as a Lineage than saying, for instance, that each of the Lineages (Frankenstein, Galeteid, Osiran, Tammuz, Ulgan, and the Extempore \u201cnon-Lineage\u201d) come in two flavors each: Fleshed and Unfleshed. <br /> <br /> Frankly, I\u2019m concerned that the concept of the Unfleshed is being narrowed to \u201cjust\u201d 1e\u2019s Tammuz: i.e., the Unfleshed are Prometheans who were created to serve. Contrast this with \u201cFrankensteins were forged out of their creator\u2019s wrath; Galeteids were created to be companions; Tammuz were created to do their masters bidding\u201d, etc \u2014 ideas which work reasonably well for both Fleshed and Unfleshed characters. <br /> <br /> Barring a clear concept for why the Unfleshed should stand as a separate Lineage, I\u2019d handle the Unfleshed by a series of sidebars: a main one describing the general concept of what an Unfleshed is in 2e, including appropriate rules modifications (e.g., what it means in game terms to be made of metal, stone, or wood rather than flesh and bone), and a separate sidebar for each Lineage explaining how the concept of the Unfleshed applies to that Lineage (e.g., how common or rare they are and what sorts of materials they tend to be made of). Possibly even allow for Fleshed/Unfleshed hybrids (e.g., a Frankenstein who was sewn together from several corpses \u2014 except for his left arm, which was crafted out of scrap metal; or a Galeteid who was carved out of marble \u2014 except for the human heart beating in her chest). <br /> <br /> More generally, I\u2019d like to see Lineages refocused from \u201chow you were made\u201d to \u201cwhy you were made\u201d.<br /> <br /> EDIT: bear in mind that I\u2019m usually very much in the \u201cwait and see\u201d camp with these things; but in this case, I\u2019m very worried about the direction that seems to be shaping up, and would like it clarified or changed before it gets too set in stone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-07-2014, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T12:25:56-07:00","id":274918,"title":"","content":"*whistles*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T12:38:21-07:00","id":274927,"title":"","content":"Matt confirmed in comments that the Galatea myth is sanitized according to the Muses. Pygmalian crafted his &quot;perfect woman&quot; from the ideal parts of other bodies. And the Tammuz are drawing much more on their Sumerian roots rather than Judaic folklore. The Unfleshed have as specific themes the whole &quot;created to be slaves&quot; element.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T13:46:00-07:00","id":274988,"title":"","content":"I will only quote <b>Dataweaver</b>'s post from other topic as it perfectly describe to me what should be made on Lineages:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/273240-ptc-2e-open-development-has-started?p=274356#post274356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aside from the ability to be more true to the original myths, one reason I\u2019m hoping that Constructs are a thing in 2e is the following excerpt from <b>Magnum Opus</b>:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Some players have difficulty with the primary theme of Promethean: attaining Humanity as a driving goal. Unlike vampire, mage and werewolf characters, the Created do not begin as human and then gain supernatural powers. Although the creation mechanics begin by creating a human being and adding supernatural, the in-character premise is quite different. Prometheans have not \u201cgone beyond\u201d humanity \u2014 they never had it. By striving to attain their Mortality, they are not giving up being super-human. They are transitioning from less-than-human to human.<br /> <br /> It may be difficult for a player to avoid thinking of his character as super-human if every Promethean character he has created or encountered was made from a human corpse. Especially for players who are familiar with <b>Vampire: The Requiem</b>, the idea of Prometheans as former humans is a difficult one to avoid. An encounter with a statue-turned-Aphrodite or a wood-carving-made-Riven may cement the concept that regardless of where their bodies came from, no Promethean is ever truly human before her Magnum Opus.</span></div>Granted, the inclusion of the Unfleshed helps immensely in this regard. OTOH,<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">Just as any legend, the tale of Galatea and Pygmalion has undergone countless retellings over the centuries. In some, Pygmalion is a king, in others, only a lonely artist. Some place the tale in Cyprus, some Rome and one legend on the island of Atlantis before its destruction. Some stories speak of the sculptor summoning forth his creation from stone, others from ivory or even wax. But the one factor that all variations of the human myth of Galatea share is that she was carved or crafted out of something inanimate, the product of an artist, not a grave-robber.</span></div>For this reason if no other, I\u2019d like Galeteids to be able to be crafted by artists. Picking a corpse that\u2019s unblemished just isn\u2019t the same as breathing life into a work of art that you crafted yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T14:23:00-07:00","id":274998,"title":"","content":"For me, the Constructs rules downplay that this is a horror setting, and that grave-robbing and corpse-mutilation is a <i>vital part of the Pilgrimage</i> drives that home. Making another vampire, in contrast, can be an act that consensual, and is completely unnecessary to the Requiem. It's a horrible act, but one that is entered into by choice, even if made in ignorance. Human bodies also keep the Prometheans secret without being the nightmare that the Masquerade imposes. That said, I find Construct rules inoffensive, and really couldn't care less whether or not they're included.<br /> <br /> Which I guess puts me on the side of pro-Construct rules, because the Unfleshed are irksome. &quot;If it's a statue, it's Unfleshed&quot;. Ugh. Statues aren't made to be slaves, they're made to be beautiful monuments to human endeavor and experience. They capture likenesses of the dead, the beautiful, the heroic, and they cement the angles and the curves of the human form in more permanent media than flesh. The Unfleshed are made to be machines. They must be fully articulated and dynamic to achieve their existential purpose, carefully engineered to not destroy themselves while operating, and are already on a path to mimicking humanity on humanity's terms. That's very different from being a living sculpture like Galatea was, and while the Golem is closer to that ideal, it actually was meant to be a slave, while an android in the modern age, right here and now, is more likely meant to be a proof-of-concept than anything else. Don't get me wrong, that's ultimately &quot;slave&quot;, but we're talking about re-creating organic structures and practical intelligence for the sake of seeing how to do so, much more in-line with the Principle than any spun-off application.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T18:36:50-07:00","id":275092,"title":"","content":"I would like to point that even if you've read it already, everyone should go back to the article and read the comments. Great questions are being asked and answered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T18:46:10-07:00","id":275096,"title":"","content":"Reading Matt's answers to people's questions it's pretty clear Muses and Golems will be made from people like in the 1.0 corebook. Also, I don't think Unfleshed are going to be built out of just anything. It seems like they'd have to serve a purpose, so like Verge said, statues and sculptures would be out.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm kind of on the fence, but I think that's more from having to readjust than anything. That being said, I dig Sumerian myth and I'm curious to see how the new non-golem Tammuz will roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T20:24:56-07:00","id":275168,"title":"","content":"I'd like to highlight something that Matt said to Wyrd for two reason. 1)I'm a self-validating prick. 2)He makes a wonderful point that counters me quite well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matthew McFarland</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There never were, though. The five Lineages presented in the core were flesh-only. Non-flesh ones weren\u2019t even mentioned until Magnum Opus and then Saturnine Night, so it\u2019s not like it\u2019s a change.<br /> <br /> That said, if you want to play a non-flesh character brought to life by one of the five Lineage methods, I\u2019m sure not gonna stop you.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T01:31:37-07:00","id":275251,"title":"","content":"Question still remains how far would the new rules be changed for enabling Constructs of classical Lineages in play? What were differences in <b>Magnum Opus</b> in 1ed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T01:40:22-07:00","id":275272,"title":"","content":"I imagine you play it the same as always, applying logic where sense calls for it-if you're playing a Ice Construct Osiran, avoid hot deserts.<br /> <br /> But it's been ages since I've read up on constructs. I should probably flip through Magnum Opus again.<br /> <br /> Well, okay, flip through Magnum opus and read something other than the Dreamborn and new Refinements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T06:06:41-07:00","id":275420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/274612-open-development-alchemical-recipes?p=275096#post275096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading Matt's answers to people's questions it's pretty clear Muses and Golems will be made from people like in the 1.0 corebook. Also, I don't think Unfleshed are going to be built out of just anything. It seems like they'd have to serve a purpose, so like Verge said, statues and sculptures would be out.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm kind of on the fence, but I think that's more from having to readjust than anything. That being said, I dig Sumerian myth and I'm curious to see how the new non-golem Tammuz will roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Sumer is fertile, untapped ground for myth stuff. I like that I have a Promethean/Werewolf connection as well. I mean, I wasn't <i>planning</i> on involving the Created in my 'wolf game, but this might be too potent an opportunity to pass up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T09:25:42-07:00","id":275502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/274612-open-development-alchemical-recipes?p=275168#post275168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to highlight something that Matt said to Wyrd for two reason. 1)I'm a self-validating prick. 2)He makes a wonderful point that counters me quite well.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think what was throwing people wasn't so much &quot;The original 5 are still flesh-only,&quot; but &quot;You can make things that aren't flesh now, but the two lines that had lots of backstory involving not being flesh aren't them.&quot; IE - People scratching their heads initially when golems were mentioned as a possible thing for Unfleshed when there was already a lineage literally referred to as Golems.<br /> <br /> Again though, with the Tammuz moving away from the Talmud and into Sumerian myth, its looking like hey're going to be pushing away from their Golem moniker. As for the Muses, the Unfleshed don't seem like they'll be encompassing magic statues, so if you want to homebrew in a marble Galatea, you're p much in the clear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T11:19:48-07:00","id":275586,"title":"","content":"Regarding Constructs and the Unfleshed as Matt describes them, I don't see that the two are incompatible. Going back to read what <i>Magnum Opus</i> says about Constructs (and seeing how much wonderful is in there that I'd forgotten!), I can see how it's a BIT of a thematic change, but to my way of seeing it, EVERY Promethean is created for a purpose. The way Matt describes the Unfleshed as a proper Lineage only makes it clear that these beings KNOW their purpose \u2013 on an abstract level through their mechanic Humour \u2013 in a way that others can only guess at, regardless of whether made by one of the established Lineages or by a human or by another Unfleshed (if that's how it works in Second Edition).<br /> <br /> ...The above notwithstanding, I appreciate Matt's sentiment of 'do it how you wanna do it' regarding these, whether we know what they even are or not!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T23:15:48-07:00","id":276107,"title":"","content":"&quot;Construct&quot; Golems, et al, could be represented by a third Bestowment for each, instead. It wouldn't throw off things too much, and the flavor of each could be kept in a well-designed and disposable character creation choice. Maybe the Tammuz gets an extra dot of Stamina, and can heal bashing/lethal with handfuls of wet clay, while the Galateid gets +1 Strength and an immunity to bashing damage attacks that don't exceed the character's Stamina.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T04:05:27-07:00","id":276161,"title":"","content":"Constructs may be things that we flesh out (tee-hee) if we do a Players Guide or something. I reread the section in <b>Magnum Opus</b> yesterday, and I like it, but they're niche cases and I'm wondering what I'm gonna have to cut to make all this fit anyway (looking at <i>you</i>, Galateids! Start pulling your weight!). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T07:06:31-07:00","id":276282,"title":"","content":"Personally, I\u2019d much rather have Constructs in the core than Extempore, which are <i>at least</i> as nich\u00e9. Which is not to say that I don\u2019t like Extempore; just that if something has to go, the guys with a worldwide population in the low single digits at best, and very likely <i>zero</i>, aren\u2019t something to which I\u2019d devote more than a mention in the core book. <br /> <br /> And while it\u2019s true that constructs don\u2019t have the same body horror to them that reanimated corpses do, neither do the Unfleshed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T07:49:28-07:00","id":276343,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, Extemporae are the option that provides a different experience. Their Humours are different, and inconsistent; Azothic Memory passes them by, but so does the baggage the other Lineages come with - less holds them back, but they less reason to hope for more than they have. Meanwhile, the Unfleshed have taken over as the &quot;made to be slaves&quot; Lineage, and expressly include pre-industrial examples. In other words, golems-as-slaves can be rendered by the Unfleshed just as easily as by the Tammuz (more so, possibly, given the changes to the Tammuz - the Tammuz now sound more like golems-as-spiritual-exercise). In other words, what is there for Constructs to be, except &quot;just like one of the other Lineages, except not flesh?&quot; With that in mind, I favour including Extemporae over Constructs. Although given that reduced side to Constructs, they could probably be rendered by little more than a Merit-like trait. In which case there'd be room for both. (Especially since most of the Lineages have some connection to the idea: golems and Galatea of course, but also Osiris wasn't raised with all his parts still biological, and the textual evidence to Frankestein is actually against the Creature being made from body parts).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T08:05:11-07:00","id":276370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/274612-open-development-alchemical-recipes?p=276161#post276161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Constructs may be things that we flesh out (tee-hee) if we do a Players Guide or something. I reread the section in <b>Magnum Opus</b> yesterday, and I like it, but they're niche cases and I'm wondering what I'm gonna have to cut to make all this fit anyway (looking at <i>you</i>, Galateids! Start pulling your weight!).</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see for the corebook all is needed small sidebar &quot;you can make Constructs, non-flesh classical Lineages members with those rules&quot; and point two, three changes - like lower conductivity of electricity in them, higher durability, more inhuman disfigurements and voila - you got yourself basic Constructs in setting. Full rules chapter aren't really needed for them right now, as changes aren't big enough from standard Prometheans, if I remember. They can have special Bestowments, detailed rules and special in-character descriptions in future books. Really, one side bar would be enough for corebook as I see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T11:11:22-07:00","id":276510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/274612-open-development-alchemical-recipes?p=276161#post276161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Constructs may be things that we flesh out (tee-hee) if we do a Players Guide or something. I reread the section in <b>Magnum Opus</b> yesterday, and I like it, but they're niche cases and I'm wondering what I'm gonna have to cut to make all this fit anyway (looking at <i>you</i>, Galateids! Start pulling your weight!).</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I'm more interested in construct fluff than construct rules. I don't think Galateids need any special rules to say they're made of marble, just the discription of the generative act that's going to be there either way.<br /> <br /> And for the record, I think that the Muses present a unique and very useful take on Promethian's core theme. It's not a splat I'd personally play, I'm generally not interested in romance plots, but I definately appreciate their presence in the game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T11:14:42-07:00","id":276512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/274612-open-development-alchemical-recipes?p=276161#post276161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(looking at <i>you</i>, Galateids! Start pulling your weight!).</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't help it. Have to post this in response:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.tate.org.uk/art/images/work/N/N05/N05955_9.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T15:34:44-07:00","id":276704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/274612-open-development-alchemical-recipes?p=276343#post276343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, Extemporae are the option that provides a different experience. Their Humours are different, and inconsistent; Azothic Memory passes them by, but so does the baggage the other Lineages come with - less holds them back, but they less reason to hope for more than they have. Meanwhile, the Unfleshed have taken over as the &amp;quot;made to be slaves&amp;quot; Lineage, and expressly include pre-industrial examples. In other words, golems-as-slaves can be rendered by the Unfleshed just as easily as by the Tammuz (more so, possibly, given the changes to the Tammuz - the Tammuz now sound more like golems-as-spiritual-exercise). In other words, what is there for Constructs to be, except &quot;just like one of the other Lineages, except not flesh?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Don\u2019t underestimate the \u201cjust like one of the other Lineages, except not flesh\u201d bit: I\u2019ve noticed a distinct tendency of readers who aren\u2019t deeply immersed in <b>Promethean</b> to think of the Created as a kind of zombie: a former human brought back to a state of unlife. Nobody <i>ever</i> thinks of an animated statue or puppet as a person who has returned from the dead; so it\u2019s much easier to think of constructs as \u201cbeings who have never been human, trying to learn about humanity\u201d. <br /> <br /> Also, I\u2019m not yet convinced that handling the Unfleshed as a Lineage of their own is a good idea: the Tammuz handled the \u201ccreated entity as slave\u201d quite well, and apparently are only being shifted away from that in 2e so as not to overlap too much with the Unfleshed Lineage; without the latter, the former can retain its slavery motif (<i>and</i> get a heavier emphasis on language; the two things aren\u2019t mutually exclusive). IMHO, another way to make space for constructs would be to ditch the Unfleshed as a separate Lineage, and instead present them as high-tech constructs (where such things as articulation, motors, sensors, and a digital brain reduce the \u201cworkload\u201d that Pyros has to deal with in animating them). What has been described thus far as a distinct \u201cUnfleshed\u201d Lineage would instead be Unfleshed Tammuz, possibly focusing on the slavery aspect more \u2014 though the software engineer in me sees potential in the language side of things, too. Conversely, there\u2019s a bit of fiction in <b>God-Machine Chronicle</b> that portrays what could be called an \u201cUnfleshed Galeteid\u201d if you go with Fleshed/Unfleshed as subtypes of the Lineages rather than five Fleshed Lineages and one Unfleshed Lineage. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/274612-open-development-alchemical-recipes?p=276343#post276343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With that in mind, I favour including Extemporae over Constructs. Although given that reduced side to Constructs, they could probably be rendered by little more than a Merit-like trait. In which case there'd be room for both. (Especially since most of the Lineages have some connection to the idea: golems and Galatea of course, but also Osiris wasn't raised with all his parts still biological, and the textual evidence to Frankestein is actually against the Creature being made from body parts).</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said before, I don\u2019t have a problem with the Extempore, and in fact would love to see them included: their \u201cmix and match\u201d nature makes them useful in other ways. For instance: if a demiurge creates a Promethean, but doesn\u2019t use any of the existing Lineages\u2019 methods when doing so, the Extempore rules could be used to represent the first Promethean of a new Lineage. Ideally, I wouldn\u2019t want to lose <i>any</i> of the three (robots, constructs, or Extempore); but Matt was saying that he already has too much in the book as is, and is going to have to cut <i>something</i> to make things fit. And if the Unfleshed are going to remain a Lineage of their own and the choice is between constructs or Extempore\u2026<br /> <br /> At the very least, if constructs don\u2019t get a write-up in the core book, I\u2019d at least like to see them get a mention \u2014 laying the ground work for them to be detailed in a supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T18:14:02-07:00","id":276878,"title":"","content":"So is there anything in this conversation beyond the battle for and against constructs?<br /> <br /> Like, has anyone noticed the awesome idea that the Lineages are <i>answers</i> to the question of life itself?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T19:20:14-07:00","id":276914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/274612-open-development-alchemical-recipes?p=276878#post276878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is there anything in this conversation beyond the battle for and against constructs?<br /> <br /> Like, has anyone noticed the awesome idea that the Lineages are <i>answers</i> to the question of life itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah we kinda got sidetracked, but the Lineages' elements being used as the source of life is a really interesting thing that I'm excited to see elaborated on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T02:53:51-07:00","id":277066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Arcane Arts:</b> Like, has anyone noticed the awesome idea that the Lineages are answers to the question of life itself? </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, I like that immensely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T04:51:39-07:00","id":277101,"title":"","content":"I haven't read anything but the core, and even that was years ago (wasn't exactly an easy sell to my university group), so I guess I didn't notice the &quot;Answer to the question of life&quot; as being particularly noteworthy.<br /> <br /> Knowing that this is a different approach to Lineages than we saw in 1E, what do you more experienced Promethean fans think the significance of the change will be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T08:14:33-07:00","id":277231,"title":"","content":"It provides a lot more punch, for starters, expanding the entire metaphor for life that Promethean already is in a lot of punch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T17:25:52-07:00","id":279185,"title":"","content":"I wonder what the Tammuz's new sobriquet will be...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T17:32:00-07:00","id":279187,"title":"","content":"Off hand guess, I bet the new &quot;Intergrity&quot; trait for Prometheans is Elpis (Hope), and reflects the degree to which they have faith in and relatively understand their Pilgrimage. At Elpis zero, with no hope at all in the New Dawn, they are lost utterly to permanent Torment.<br /> <br /> Centimani would presumably relate differently to what they have hope in (I understand them not being considered a Refinement, but I hope mechanics still treat them as one for the purpose of adopting the path, and some Centimani and others may even consider it one - the fact that the Centimani glyph incorporates the alchemical symbol for Sulfer always struck me as a meaningful choice).<br /> <br /> Ideally, different Refinements would provide different types of Breakingpoints and Touchstones for Elpis while you're on that Refinement. Because under the previous system their was an obvious bias toward Aurum with &quot;Humanity&quot; being so intricate to the New Dawn. But if your grotesque experimentations with life and death, or whatever, can serve your Elpis as it wouldn't have your Humanity previously, provided its part of the right Refinement, it would go a long way to removing that artificially &quot;moral&quot; element from the Pilgrimage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-12-2014, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T20:56:04-07:00","id":279340,"title":"","content":"I hope the organ associations of the different humours change a bit this time. I mean, I know different medieval texts associate them differently, but I think this line up would be more accurate to humourous alchemy in general...<br /> <br /> Choleric - Spleen<br /> Melancholic - Gall bladder<br /> Phlegmatic - Lungs<br /> Sanguine - Liver<br /> <br /> Ectoplasmic - Pineal Gland","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}